{% comment %}
  Collection description — the pinned note under the grid.

  Howard writes several hundred words per collection for search. Above the
  products that copy is the whole first screen on mobile and the grid never
  gets seen, so the page splits it: `ll-collection-header` carries a one-line
  intro with a "Read more ↓" jump, and the body lands here on aged paper
  below the grid.

  The text is `collection.description` verbatim — same field, same admin box,
  nothing for Howard to keep in two places. It is in the markup in full on
  every render, so a crawler reads the same words as someone who never opens
  the disclosure.

  Desktop and mobile are one DOM, reshaped in CSS rather than duplicated:

    desktop — the whole block is the paper card (760px, hairline, hard
              shadow), heading row inside it above a dashed seam, full copy
    mobile  — heading row steps outside and above the card, the card holds
              the lead paragraph, and the rest sits behind the Read more row

  So `__inner` wears the card chrome on desktop and `__card` wears it on
  mobile. Neither is decoration for its own sake — the disclosure is what
  keeps the footer reachable on a phone.

  The collapse is CSS, not measurement: `mobile_lead` blocks stay visible and
  the siblings after them are `display: none` until `data-expanded` flips.
  `<ll-expandable-text>` only carries that flag and hides the toggle when
  there is nothing behind it. Nothing is inserted, moved or removed, which is
  why arbitrary rich text survives it.

  `normalise_alignment` exists because Shopify's rich text editor writes
  `text-align` as an inline style per paragraph, and a lot of the current
  descriptions are centred from when they sat under a centred heading.
  Centred long prose is hard to read and inline styles beat any stylesheet,
  so the override has to be `!important` to reach them.

  Nothing renders when the description is empty, so the section can sit in
  `templates/collection.json` for every collection without leaving a gap on
  the ones Howard has not written yet. One instance per template: the anchor
  id is fixed so the header's jump link has something stable to aim at.
{% endcomment %}

<script
  src="{{ 'll-expandable-text.js' | asset_url }}"
  type="module"
  fetchpriority="low"
></script>

{%- liquid
  assign section_settings = section.settings
  assign description = collection.description

  # `[collection]` is spelled out in the setting's help text. Liquid in a
  # theme setting is not evaluated, so a token is the only way to let Howard
  # write one heading that reads correctly on every collection.
  assign heading = section_settings.heading | replace: '[collection]', collection.title

  if section_settings.background_color != blank
    render 'contrast-override', background_color: section_settings.background_color, section_id: section.id
  endif
-%}

{%- if description != blank -%}
  <div
    class="section-background ll-collection-description__band{% if section_settings.show_top_rule %} ll-collection-description__band--ruled{% endif %}{% if section_settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}"
  ></div>
  <div
    class="section section--page-width ll-collection-description spacing-style{% if section_settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}"
    id="collection-description"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section_settings %}"
  >
    <ll-expandable-text
      class="ll-collection-description__inner"
      data-lead="{{ section_settings.mobile_lead }}"
    >
      {%- if heading != blank or section_settings.show_aside -%}
        <div class="ll-collection-description__header">
          {%- if heading != blank -%}
            <h2 class="ll-collection-description__heading">{{ heading }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Katie's pen, same block as everywhere else. Its own text rather
            than `custom.hand_aside` — that metafield is spoken for by the
            aside beside the collection title, and the design gives this one a
            different line ("a bit of background").
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if section_settings.show_aside -%}
            {% content_for 'block', type: 'll-hand-aside', id: 'aside' %}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="ll-collection-description__card">
        <div
          class="ll-collection-description__body rte{% if section_settings.normalise_alignment %} ll-collection-description__body--start{% endif %}"
          id="collection-description-body"
        >
          {{ description }}
        </div>

        {%- if section_settings.collapse_on_mobile -%}
          <button
            class="ll-collection-description__toggle"
            type="button"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="collection-description-body"
            data-ll-expandable-toggle
          >
            <span class="ll-collection-description__toggle-label" data-when="collapsed">
              {{- section_settings.more_label | escape -}}
            </span>
            <span class="ll-collection-description__toggle-label" data-when="expanded">
              {{- section_settings.less_label | escape -}}
            </span>
            {%- comment -%}
              Decorative: the label already says which way this goes, so the
              chevron is kept out of the accessibility tree rather than read
              out twice.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="ll-collection-description__toggle-caret" aria-hidden="true">
              <span data-when="collapsed">&rsaquo;</span>
              <span data-when="expanded">&#8964;</span>
            </span>
          </button>

          {%- comment -%}
            The collapse is applied in CSS so there is no flash of the full
            block on load, which means a reader with JS off would be left with
            a lead paragraph and a dead button. Open it up for them.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <noscript>
            <style>
              .ll-collection-description__body > * {
                display: revert !important;
              }

              .ll-collection-description__toggle {
                display: none !important;
              }
            </style>
          </noscript>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </ll-expandable-text>
  </div>
{%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
  <div class="section section--page-width ll-collection-description">
    <p class="ll-collection-description__placeholder">
      This collection has no description yet. Add one in Products → Collections and it will appear
      here. The section stays hidden on the live site until then.
    </p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .ll-collection-description__band--ruled {
    border-block-start: var(--ll-stitch);
  }

  /* The header's "Read more ↓" lands here, so clear the sticky header. */
  .ll-collection-description {
    scroll-margin-block-start: calc(var(--header-group-height, 0px) + 16px);
  }

  .ll-collection-description__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;

    /* Desktop: the wrapper is the card. Mobile swaps this onto `__card` so the
       heading can step outside it — see the media query. */
    max-width: 47.5rem; /* 760px */
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 36px 40px 40px;
    background-color: var(--ll-paper-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--ll-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--ll-radius-tight);
    /* Lighter than --ll-shadow-offset: this card is a note on the page, not a
       product tile lifted off it. */
    box-shadow: 2px 3px 0 rgb(46 42 36 / 0.1);
  }

  .ll-collection-description__header {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 14px;
    padding-block-end: 14px;
    border-block-end: var(--ll-stitch);
  }

  .ll-collection-description__heading {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.5rem; /* 24px — a footnote to the grid, not a second title */
  }

  .ll-collection-description__card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .ll-collection-description__body {
    margin-block-start: 16px;
    color: var(--ll-peat);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* `.rte` sets its own heading rhythm off the body scale; this copy is set to
     the design's spacing instead, and the subheads are Bevan like every other
     heading on the site. */
  .ll-collection-description__body > * {
    margin-block: 0 16px;
  }

  .ll-collection-description__body :is(h2, h3, h4, h5, h6) {
    margin-block: 24px 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: var(--font-heading--weight);
    font-size: 1.0625rem; /* 17px */
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--ll-ink);
  }

  .ll-collection-description__body > :first-child {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  .ll-collection-description__body > :last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  /* Reaches inline `text-align` written by the rich text editor. See the note
     at the top of the file — a stylesheet cannot outrank an inline style
     without this. */
  .ll-collection-description__body--start :is(p, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, ul, ol, li, blockquote) {
    text-align: start !important;
  }

  /* Desktop shows the copy whole; the disclosure is a mobile answer to a
     mobile problem, so the control does not exist above 750px. */
  .ll-collection-description__toggle {
    display: none;
  }

  .ll-collection-description__placeholder {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-accent--family);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--ll-peat);
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ll-collection-description__inner {
      gap: 14px;

      /* Chrome moves to `__card`; the wrapper goes back to being a wrapper. */
      max-width: none;
      padding: 0;
      background-color: transparent;
      border: 0;
      box-shadow: none;
    }

    /* Stacked and outside the card, so the Caveat line sits under the heading
       rather than beside it. */
    .ll-collection-description__header {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 2px;
      padding-block-end: 0;
      border-block-end: 0;
    }

    .ll-collection-description__heading {
      font-size: 1.3125rem; /* 21px */
    }

    .ll-collection-description__card {
      padding: 18px 18px 6px;
      background-color: var(--ll-paper-card);
      border: 1px solid var(--ll-border-strong);
      border-radius: var(--ll-radius-tight);
    }

    .ll-collection-description__body {
      margin-block-start: 0;
      font-size: 0.9375rem; /* 15px */
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .ll-collection-description__body > * {
      margin-block: 0 14px;
    }

    .ll-collection-description__body :is(h2, h3, h4, h5, h6) {
      margin-block: 20px 14px;
      font-size: 1rem; /* 16px */
    }

    /* The collapse itself: everything past the lead is out of the flow, and
       out of the accessibility tree with it, until the toggle flips. */
    ll-expandable-text:not([data-expanded='true']) .ll-collection-description__body > * + * {
      display: none;
    }

    ll-expandable-text[data-lead='2']:not([data-expanded='true'])
      .ll-collection-description__body
      > :nth-child(-n + 2) {
      display: revert;
    }

    ll-expandable-text[data-lead='3']:not([data-expanded='true'])
      .ll-collection-description__body
      > :nth-child(-n + 3) {
      display: revert;
    }

    .ll-collection-description__toggle {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      width: 100%;
      /* 44px is the tap target; the row is the full width of the card so the
         whole seam is pressable, as drawn. */
      min-height: 44px;
      margin-block-start: 2px;
      padding: 0;
      background: none;
      border: 0;
      border-block-start: var(--ll-stitch);
      font-family: var(--font-body--family);
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: 0.875rem; /* 14px */
      color: var(--ll-moor);
      text-align: start;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .ll-collection-description__toggle-caret {
      font-size: 1.0625rem; /* 17px */
      line-height: 1;
    }

    /* Only one label and one chevron are true at a time. */
    .ll-collection-description__toggle [data-when='expanded'],
    ll-expandable-text[data-expanded='true'] .ll-collection-description__toggle [data-when='collapsed'] {
      display: none;
    }

    ll-expandable-text[data-expanded='true'] .ll-collection-description__toggle [data-when='expanded'] {
      display: inline;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection description",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["collection"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows the collection's description from Products → Collections. On mobile everything past the opening paragraph sits behind a Read more row so the copy does not bury the footer."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Use [collection] for the collection name. Leave empty for no heading.",
      "default": "More about our [collection]"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_aside",
      "label": "Show handwritten note",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_top_rule",
      "label": "Show stitched rule above",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "normalise_alignment",
      "label": "Align text to the left",
      "info": "Overrides centring applied in the collection description editor. Long text is easier to read left aligned.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Mobile"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "collapse_on_mobile",
      "label": "Collapse behind Read more",
      "info": "Mobile only. The full text is always present for search engines.",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "mobile_lead",
      "label": "Paragraphs shown before Read more",
      "info": "Raise this if your description opens with a short bold line.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "1",
          "label": "1"
        },
        {
          "value": "2",
          "label": "2"
        },
        {
          "value": "3",
          "label": "3"
        }
      ],
      "default": "1"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "more_label",
      "label": "Expand label",
      "default": "Read more"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "less_label",
      "label": "Collapse label",
      "default": "Read less"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.colors"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:settings.background_color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default",
      "default": "#efe7d2"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 56
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 64
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Collection description",
      "category": "Lighthouse Lane",
      "blocks": {
        "aside": {
          "type": "ll-hand-aside",
          "static": true,
          "settings": {
            "source": "text",
            "text": "a bit of background",
            "font_size": "1.1875rem",
            "rotation": -1
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
